      "text": "To solve for the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\), we need to use the information given about the angles in the diagram and apply the properties of a straight line and angles at a point.\n\n1. **Understanding the Diagram:**\n   - We have a straight line \\(SP\\).\n   - \\(\\angle QSP = 80^\\circ\\).\n   - Since \\(SP\\) is a straight line, the adjacent angle at \\(S\\) (which is \\(\\angle QSP\\)) and the angle on the straight line must sum up to \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Identifying Supplementary Angles:**\n   - The angle at \\(S\\) on the straight line, \\(\\angle QSR\\), is supplementary to \\(\\angle QSP\\).\n   - Therefore, \\(\\angle QSR = 180^\\circ - \\angle QSP = 180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = 100^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Using the Angle Sum Property:**\n   - The angles around point \\(R\\) on the straight line add up to \\(180^\\circ\\).\n   - Let \\(\\angle PQR = x\\).\n\n4. **Formulating the Equation:**\n   - The sum of the angles forming the straight line, \\(\\angle QSR\\), \\(\\angle PSR\\), and \\(\\angle PQR\\) should equal \\(180^\\circ\\).\n   - \\(\\angle PSR\\) is a right angle, which is \\(90^\\circ\\), because \\(SP\\) is a straight line.\n   - Therefore, \\(100^\\circ + 90^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\\).\n\n5. **Solving for \\(x\\):**\n   \\[\n   100^\\circ + 90^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   190^\\circ + x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 180^\\circ - 190^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = -10^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle PQR\\) is \\(\\boxed{80}\\).",
